cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the size-decision-general model or build on this report, please cite it as below."
title: "A calibrated encoder classifier as the cost floor for production decisions"
abstract: >-
  Technical report for size-decision-general, a 307M-parameter non-autoregressive
  encoder classifier that answers option-list questions in a single forward pass
  and returns a calibrated probability distribution (ECE under 0.06 on three
  public classification benchmarks). It is positioned as the cheap, deterministic
  high-throughput layer beneath generative decoders, where calibrated confidence
  enables gating on probability rather than only on the argmax.
type: report
